StupidMirror uses Apple platform APIs, including CoreMediaIO and AVFoundation,
to discover and render USB iPhone screen sources exposed by macOS.

Optional device control support relies on Appium, WebDriverAgent, and
UiAutomator2, which are separate projects with their own licenses and setup
requirements.

Android mirroring uses the scrcpy server from the scrcpy project. The scrcpy
server, Appium, WebDriverAgent, and UiAutomator2 remain subject to their
respective upstream licenses.

The bundled `smtunnel` device tunnel sidecar (tools/smtunnel) is built with
go-ios (github.com/danielpaulus/go-ios, MIT License) and gVisor's netstack
(gvisor.dev/gvisor, Apache License 2.0), plus their Go module dependencies.
Those components remain subject to their own licenses; see
tools/smtunnel/go.mod for the exact versions.

The Codex preview UI adapts iPhone Use (https://github.com/zhongerxin/iPhone-use,
MIT License) and bundles the MCP Apps SDK. Attribution and license texts are in
plugins/stupidmirror/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and assets/widget-licenses.txt.
The smpreview WebRTC sidecar uses Pion and its Go dependencies; exact versions
are in tools/smpreview/go.mod and license texts in
plugins/stupidmirror/assets/webrtc-licenses.txt.

App updates use Sparkle (https://sparkle-project.org, MIT License), embedded as
Sparkle.framework. Its license text ships in the app as
Resources/Sparkle-LICENSE.txt and is kept in Assets/licenses/Sparkle-LICENSE.txt.
